{"name":"Painite","hex":"#6b4947","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"painite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very rare orange-red borate mineral consisting mostly of calcium, zirconium, boron, aluminium, and oxygen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/painite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Painite","blocks":[{"text":"Painite is a rare borate mineral. It was first found in Myanmar by British mineralogist and gem dealer Arthur C.D. Pain who misidentified it as ruby, until it was discovered as a new gemstone in the 1950s. When it was confirmed as a new mineral species, the mineral was named after him."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Painite2.jpg/330px-Painite2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Painite","wikidata":"Q419868"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Painite-266170.jpg/250px-Painite-266170.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Painite-266170.jpg/330px-Painite-266170.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Painite-266170.jpg/250px-Painite-266170.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APainite-266170.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Painite-255206.jpg/250px-Painite-255206.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Painite-255206.jpg/330px-Painite-255206.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/Painite-255206.jpg/250px-Painite-255206.jpg?utm_source=en.w